- Save to uploads/pcaps</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>Relation</id><coordinates><x>279</x><y>131</y><w>27</w><h>72</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>lt=&lt;&lt;-</panel_attributes><additional_attributes>10;60;10;10</additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLClass</id><coordinates><x>216</x><y>185</y><w>315</w><h>135</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>halign=left
Parse pcap with scapy:
for packet in file:
 - Extract packet_number (index)
 - Extract timestamp
 - Extract src_ip and dst_ip
 - Extract src_port and dst_port (if TCP/UDP)
 - Extract protocol (TCP, UDP, ICMP, OTHER)
 - Extract packet_length
 - Extract packet_data (bytes)</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>Relation</id><coordinates><x>279</x><y>311</y><w>108</w><h>81</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>lt=&lt;&lt;-
